WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
A night sky, clear and full of stars.

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.330
A figure walks across it,
and never turns to face us.

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.780
"She walks in Beauty, like
the night" Words drift in,

4
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.900
one by one: night, starry, dark, bright.

5
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.500
A slider moves between
dark and bright, and stops,

6
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.220
exactly in the middle.

7
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.700
It's a love poem, yet it
hardly mentions her body.

8
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.470
So what is it praising?

9
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.680
In this mission, you'll ask why
Byron compares her to the night.

10
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.130
You'll weigh how the poem
sets dark against bright.

11
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.360
And you'll follow its three
stanzas, written in June 1814,

12
00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.710
from the first line to the last.

13
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:46.120
Your mission: work out
what the poem is praising.
